From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cennac <cennac@163.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: disable APCF after controller rejection

The AP6275P vendor-capability response advertises advertising-packet content
filtering, but its LE_ADV_FILTER READ_EXTENDED_FEATURES subcommand completes
with INVALID_HCI_COMMAND_PARAMETERS. The current stack logs that status and
keeps `is_filter_supported_` enabled. A later Settings discovery sends APCF
ENABLE, waits for opcode 0xfd57, times out, and aborts the Bluetooth process.

Treat a rejected or malformed extended-features response as an authoritative
runtime downgrade. This keeps ordinary LE scanning usable on controllers whose
static vendor capabilities are too optimistic.

Test: manual r7 reproduction: enable Bluetooth, start Settings discovery, and
verify no second LE_ADV_FILTER command or process restart.
---
 system/gd/hci/le_scanning_manager.cc | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/system/gd/hci/le_scanning_manager.cc b/system/gd/hci/le_scanning_manager.cc
index 7301d805c1..fd13238cb3 100644
--- a/system/gd/hci/le_scanning_manager.cc
+++ b/system/gd/hci/le_scanning_manager.cc
@@ -1462,15 +1462,21 @@ class LeScanningManager::impl : public LeAddressManagerCallback {
   void on_apcf_read_extended_features_complete(CommandCompleteView view) {
     ASSERT(view.IsValid());
     auto status_view = LeAdvFilterCompleteView::Create(view);
     if (!status_view.IsValid()) {
-      LOG_WARN("Can not get valid LeAdvFilterCompleteView, return");
+      LOG_WARN("Invalid LeAdvFilterCompleteView; disabling APCF support");
+      is_filter_supported_ = false;
+      is_transport_discovery_data_filter_supported_ = false;
+      is_ad_type_filter_supported_ = false;
       return;
     }
     if (status_view.GetStatus() != ErrorCode::SUCCESS) {
-      LOG_WARN(
-          "Got a Command complete %s, status %s",
-          OpCodeText(view.GetCommandOpCode()).c_str(),
-          ErrorCodeText(status_view.GetStatus()).c_str());
+      LOG_WARN(
+          "Got a Command complete %s, status %s; disabling APCF support",
+          OpCodeText(view.GetCommandOpCode()).c_str(),
+          ErrorCodeText(status_view.GetStatus()).c_str());
+      is_filter_supported_ = false;
+      is_transport_discovery_data_filter_supported_ = false;
+      is_ad_type_filter_supported_ = false;
       return;
     }
     auto complete_view = LeAdvFilterReadExtendedFeaturesCompleteView::Create(status_view);
